 excluding what it rules out (a normal MRI excludes both imaging items; a normal CT excludes atrophy only). Contradictions, left 'not reported' in the checklist and reported in phenotypic_features only where both statements are individual-level: B.E. walks with an 'unsteady gait' yet 'did not show ataxia or hypotonia'; I.C. had a 30-word vocabulary but did not combine words while the Discussion calls his speech and language normal; N.O. has pallidal hyperintensity in the text while block 2 says 'MRI probably normal?'; T.A. had 'Two EEGs and MRI were normal' while cranial CT 'raised the ques- tion of cerebellar atrophy'. P.S.H.'s age at death is 13 years in the Methods and 13!/2 years in her own case report. K.S. is not a contradiction (normal MRI in 1992; globus pallidus, thalamus and brain-stem lesions in February 1996). P.L.'s hypotonia resolved by 13 months but is recorded observed. D.E.'s hedged 'He may have had a few very short astatic seizures' was not counted as observed. The paper hyphenates many words across PDF line breaks with a character that is not a plain space, so spans were chosen to avoid those points wherever possible; for Y.A.'s EEG, whose sentence is hyphenated at every keyword, the span is given as two short clean fragments. No ALDH5A1 variant is printed anywhere: the gene appears only as 'The SSADH gene is single copy and has been mapped to chromosome 6p23.7', no molecular testing of patients is reported, and every diagnosis rests on urinary organic acid analysis plus enzyme activity, so no variant is tied to any person and the variants table is empty. is_proband is false for everyone with a null span: no person is called the proband or index case (the only occurrence is the cohort phrase 'Approximately 40% of the probands in this report'). Ages printed in garbled OCR form ('3V2 y', '4 ]/2 y', '9lA y', '6% y', '7&gt;h years', '13l/2 years', '7Vi years', '4}/i years') were kept verbatim with a null ISO 8601 value. Labels use the paper's own initials; K.S. comes from the case report although the table prints 'ICS.', and I.O. is labelled from the table row because the case-report text prints 'LO.'. Relatives: the three relatives for whom the paper gives an individual-level fact got rows (the mother of P.S.H., the maternal sister of I.C., the paternal cousin of I.C.); relatives described only as healthy or well, or as a bare group ('three siblings who are well', 'two older, healthy siblings', 'an older sister who is healthy', 'a healthy, older male sibling', 'two other children, a 16-year-old and a 14-year-old, who were healthy'), were given no rows because the paper gives no individual-level clinical fact about any of them - a judgement call. HPO candidates were left null.",
